note sh_mix_wrap: a uchar value shifted by a ulong amount of 256 traps 7 (exit 107) in omc: the amount is
note compared whole, never wrapped to the value's 8 bits (that would be a shift by 0). "a\n" comes first.
text t "a\n"
fn shw a uchar s ulong to uchar
ret shl a s
end
fn main to int
w = write 1 t 0 2
x = shw 1 256
ret int x
end
